 "observations": [
  "The page number «170» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 58a», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature. The titles (L01-L02), as on p. 169 (JP2 0201): «Tabula elgeib (O)» and «[Tabula sinus]», in bold, the siglum in roman. The folios of the manuscripts stand at the left of the titles in two lines, «C 72r, O 129v,» and «N 38v.», the letters raised; here as left margin notes. Specks in the margins; not transcribed.",
  "The table: one half of the table of p. 169, eight columns of arguments and three of the sine, divided by a double vertical rule; the heads «Semitae numerorum (CO) Lineae numeri (N)» and «Elgeib (CO) Sinus (N)», the units «Sig.» and «Gr.» four times and «Part.», «Min.», «Sec.» without notes, in smaller bold type. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L03-L05), the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The arguments are 2s x, 3s (30 − x), 8s x and 9s (30 − x) for x = 61° to 89° (2s 1° to 2s 29°), the last row 3s 0°, 3s 0°, 9s 0°, 9s 0° for 90° and 270°.",
  "L06-L35. Checked: each sine is 60 · sin x to within 1.1″, and 60p 0′ 0″ at 90°: within 0.8″ in every row except at 83° and 85°, 59p 33′ 11″ and 59p 46′ 19″ for 59p 33′ 10.0″ and 59p 46′ 18.1″. Compared with al-Battānī's sine table (Nallino, II, 56) the values agree except at 63°, 65°, 74°, 80° and 84°, where al-Khwārizmī's value is 1″ less, and at 83° and 87°, where it is 1″ more; al-Battānī's value is the nearer to the computation at 74°, 83° and 84°, al-Khwārizmī's at 63°, 65°, 80° and 87°.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked: the edition's readings are al-Battānī's values and those of the computation within 1″: the minutes 58 at 62° (note a, against the 38 of O and N and C's 28), C's seconds 37 there (note b, against O's 27), 52p 58′ 36.7″ computed; C's minutes 37 at 68° (note c, against the 38 of O and N), 55p 37′ 51.7″ computed; and the seconds 19 at 85° (note d, against the 17 of C and O), where 59p 46′ 18.1″ is computed: the manuscripts' 17 is 1.1″ from the computation and 2″ from al-Battānī's 19, the value the edition takes by Suter's rule (p. 69, JP2 0101, L40-L44)."
